## Findings for the docs
1. Docs say "Python 3.12" but not what to do when the system Python differs (Codespace
   default was 3.14). Suggested README line: "If your system Python isn't 3.12, use Docker
   or `uv venv --python 3.12`."
2. Alembic prints nothing on startup (no logging config in `alembic.ini`), so a successful
   migration is silent. Verify with `SHOW TABLES`.
3. `docker compose up` creates `frontend/node_modules` owned by root (bind mount), so a
   later host-side `npm ci` fails with EACCES. Fix: `sudo rm -rf frontend/node_modules`,
   or run host npm checks before starting Docker.
4. `npm ci` reports 14 vulnerabilities (8 moderate, 4 high, 2 critical) and a deprecated
   ESLint 9.39.5. Not part of S1-005; worth a separate dependency-update ticket.
5. The Codespaces URL isn't an authorized Firebase domain and CORS allows only
   `localhost:5173`, so sign-in can't be tested there.
